      "title": "Coefficient of Variation: Formula and Examples",
      "url": "https://www.investopedia.com/terms/c/coefficientofvariation.asp",
      "snippet": "The coefficient of variation is calculated as standard deviation divided by mean, often multiplied by 100 to express a percentage. For example, a standard deviation of 2 and a mean of 10 gives a CV of 20%.",
      "domain": "investopedia.com",
      "rank": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "Python Standard Deviation: population vs sample",
      "url": "https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/python/python-standard-deviation/",
      "snippet": "In Python, population standard deviation can be computed with `statistics.pstdev()` or `numpy.std(..., ddof=0)`, while sample standard deviation uses `statistics.stdev()` or `ddof=1`. A 4-value dataset like [2, 4, 4, 4] has a population standard deviation of about 0.866.",
      "domain": "geeksforgeeks.org",
      "rank": 3
    },
