      "title": "numpy.std \u2014 NumPy v2.0 Manual",
      "url": "https://numpy.org/doc/stable/reference/generated/numpy.std.html",
      "snippet": "`numpy.std()` computes the standard deviation along a specified axis and defaults to `ddof=0`, which is the population standard deviation. The result can be combined with `numpy.mean()` to calculate coefficient of variation as `std / mean`.",
      "domain": "numpy.org",
      "rank": 4
    },
    {
      "title": "Coefficient of Variation in Python using NumPy and Statistics",
      "url": "https://www.simplilearn.com/tutorials/python-tutorial/coefficient-of-variation-in-python",
      "snippet": "The coefficient of variation formula is `CV = (standard deviation / mean) \u00d7 100`. In Python, you can use `statistics.pstdev()` for population standard deviation and then divide by `statistics.mean()` to get a percentage such as 12.5% for a 1.25 SD and a 10 mean.",
      "domain": "simplilearn.com",
      "rank": 5
    }
  ],
  "query": "Python population standard deviation coefficient of variation formula",
