      "title": "Self-Attention with Relative Position Representations",
      "url": "https://aclanthology.org/N18-2074/",
      "snippet": "Peter Shaw, Jakob Uszkoreit, and Ashish Vaswani presented a self-attention variant that adds relative position representations to improve sequence modeling. Published in 2018, the paper is frequently cited in work on efficient attention and long-context Transformer models.",
      "domain": "aclanthology.org",
      "rank": 2
    },
    {
      "title": "Generating Long Sequences with Sparse Transformers",
      "url": "https://aclanthology.org/P19-1285/",
      "snippet": "Rewon Child, Scott Gray, Alec Radford, and Ilya Sutskever proposed sparse attention patterns to reduce the quadratic cost of standard Transformer attention. The 2019 paper shows that carefully designed sparse self-attention can scale to sequences with tens of thousands of tokens.",
      "domain": "aclanthology.org",
      "rank": 3
    },
    {
      "title": "Linformer: Self-Attention with Linear Complexity",
      "url": "https://aclanthology.org/2020.acl-main.592/",
      "snippet": "Sinong Wang, Belinda Z. Li, Madian Khabsa, Han Fang, and Han Hu introduced Linformer at ACL 2020. Their method approximates self-attention with low-rank projections and claims linear-time and linear-space complexity in sequence length.",
      "domain": "aclanthology.org",
      "rank": 4
    },
    {
      "title": "Transformers are RNNs: Fast Autoregressive Transformers with Linear Attention",
      "url": "https://aclanthology.org/2020.emnlp-main.33/",
      "snippet": "James T. Ryan, Mitchell Stern, and Noah A. Smith described linear attention methods that make autoregressive Transformers more efficient for long sequences. The EMNLP 2020 paper compares standard softmax attention against kernelized alternatives and reports substantial memory savings.",
      "domain": "aclanthology.org",
      "rank": 5
    }
  ],
  "query": "site:aclanthology.org transformer attention paper highly cited self-attention efficient attention authors year",
  "count": 5
}

